  "content": {
    "id": "p26-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Find, in factored form, the equations of the parabolas with the given intercepts.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 4,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p26-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x=1,3$\n\n$y=6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=2(x-1)(x-3)$",
          "worked": "The zeroes give $y=a(x-1)(x-3)$. Substitute the $y$-intercept $(0,6)$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}6&=a(0-1)(0-3)\\\\6&=3a\\\\a&=2\\\\y&=2(x-1)(x-3)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x=-2,1$\n\n$y=4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=-2(x+2)(x-1)$",
          "worked": "The zeroes give $y=a(x+2)(x-1)$. Substitute the $y$-intercept $(0,4)$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}4&=a(0+2)(0-1)\\\\4&=-2a\\\\a&=-2\\\\y&=-2(x+2)(x-1)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$x=-1,5$\n\n$y=15$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=-3(x+1)(x-5)$",
          "worked": "The zeroes give $y=a(x+1)(x-5)$. Substitute the $y$-intercept $(0,15)$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}15&=a(0+1)(0-5)\\\\15&=-5a\\\\a&=-3\\\\y&=-3(x+1)(x-5)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q12-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$x=-2,-4$\n\n$y=2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=\\frac14(x+2)(x+4)$",
          "worked": "The zeroes give $y=a(x+2)(x+4)$. Substitute the $y$-intercept $(0,2)$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2&=a(0+2)(0+4)\\\\2&=8a\\\\a&=\\frac14\\\\y&=\\frac14(x+2)(x+4)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      }
    ]
